>
  <p>
    This policy covers all apps published by Rubens Pessoa de Barros Filho e.U &mdash; currently
    <strong>Save My Cactus</strong>, <strong>Hustlrr</strong>, <strong>Giorni</strong>, and
    <strong>Appelou</strong> &mdash; and this website. It explains what data is processed, why,
    who processes it, and the rights you have.
  </p>
  <p>
    The short version: the apps work without accounts, your content stays on your device (and in
    your own iCloud, if you use it), payments run through Apple, and we do not sell your personal
    data.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    Rubens Pessoa de Barros Filho e.U
    <br />
    UNESCO-Esplanade 8/55, 8020 Graz, Austria
    <br />
    Email: <a href="mailto:contact@rubenspessoa.dev">contact@rubenspessoa.dev</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    See the <a href="/imprint/">imprint</a> for full legal details.
  </p>

  <h2>What each app processes</h2>

  <h3>Save My Cactus</h3>
  <p>
    When you identify or diagnose a plant, your photo is sent to our servers and processed through
    the API of a specialized third-party AI service, solely to generate the result. The photo
    carries no account identifier, is not used to train AI models under our API agreements, and is
    not stored on our servers: it is processed in memory and discarded. Photos you save in the app
    stay on your device and in your own iCloud. The app creates an anonymous identifier via
    Firebase to enforce fair usage limits and connect your subscription to your installation; we
    cannot identify you personally from it.
  </p>

  <h3>Hustlrr</h3>
  <p>
    The content of your conversations &mdash; text, uploaded documents, and text transcribed from
    voice input &mdash; is sent through our servers to the AI provider behind the model you
    selected (currently OpenAI and Anthropic), solely to generate the response. This content is
    not used to train AI models under our API agreements, and our servers do not keep a copy of
    your conversations. Your chat history is stored on your device and, if you use iCloud, synced
    through your own private iCloud storage. Requests are verified with Firebase App Check to keep
    bots away; no account is involved.
  </p>

  <h3>Giorni</h3>
  <p>
    Your habits, completions, focus sessions, and notes stay on your device and, if you use
    iCloud, in your own private iCloud storage. We operate no server for Giorni, and reminders are
    local notifications scheduled on your device. Analytics events (feature usage, not the content
    of your habits) are the only data that leaves the app.
  </p>

  <h3>Appelou</h3>
  <p>
    Your product searches are sent to our servers to return matching offers. With your permission,
    the app uses your device location to show offers from stores near you; location is used at
    query time and is not stored as a movement history. The free tier shows ads served by Google
    AdMob: if you allow tracking in the iOS App Tracking Transparency prompt, ads may be
    personalized; if you decline, they are not. AppsFlyer processes device identifiers to
    attribute app installs to marketing campaigns, subject to the same tracking choice.
  </p>

  <h3>This website and app websites</h3>
  <p>
    This website (rubenspessoa.dev) is static and sets no cookies and runs no analytics. Some app
    websites use analytics and, where required, ask for cookie consent; their processing is
    covered by the services listed below.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    We keep the list of processors as small as each app allows. Not every service is used by every
    app:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Apple (USA): App Store distribution, payments, device services, iCloud</li>
    <li>
      Google Firebase (USA/Ireland): server infrastructure (Cloud Functions), app verification
      (App Check), analytics, and crash reporting (Crashlytics)
    </li>
    <li>RevenueCat (USA): subscription status, keyed to anonymous identifiers</li>
    <li>OpenAI (USA) and Anthropic (USA): generating responses in Hustlrr</li>
    <li>AI service providers (USA): analysis of plant photos in Save My Cactus</li>
    <li>PostHog (EU-hosted): product analytics for Save My Cactus</li>
    <li>TelemetryDeck (Germany): anonymized product analytics for Hustlrr and Giorni</li>
    <li>Amplitude (USA): product analytics for Giorni</li>
    <li>Sentry (USA): crash and error reporting for Hustlrr</li>
    <li>Google AdMob (USA): advertising in Appelou</li>
    <li>AppsFlyer (USA/EU) and Adjust (Germany): install attribution</li>
    <li>Algolia (USA): product search in Appelou</li>
    <li>Google Analytics (USA/Ireland): analytics on some app websites</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Legal bases</h2>
  <p>
    Under the GDPR (and the corresponding bases of the Brazilian LGPD) we process data based on:
    <strong>performance of a contract</strong> (providing the app features you use and your
    subscription), <strong>legitimate interest</strong> (product analytics, crash reporting, abuse
    prevention, non-personalized ads), <strong>consent</strong> (location access, personalized
    advertising, tracking-based attribution), and <strong>legal obligation</strong> where
    applicable.
  </p>

  <h2>International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Where providers are located in the USA or other countries outside the EU, transfers rely on
    the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, Standard Contractual Clauses, or equivalent safeguards
    (including those recognized by the LGPD for users in Brazil).
  </p>

  <h2>How long data is kept</h2>
  <p>
    Personal data is processed and stored only as long as required by the purpose it was collected
    for: photos and conversations are not retained on our servers at all; rate-limit and usage
    counters expire automatically within days; analytics, attribution, and crash data follow the
    retention settings of the respective tool. Once the retention period expires, data is deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you have the right to access, rectify, delete, restrict, or
    receive a copy of your data, to object to processing based on legitimate interest, and to
    withdraw consent at any time (for tracking and location, directly in iOS Settings).
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>EU/EEA and Switzerland:</strong> the rights above under the GDPR and Swiss FADP, and
      the right to complain to the Austrian Data Protection Authority (
      <a href="https://www.dsb.gv.at" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">dsb.gv.at</a>) or
      your local supervisory authority.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Brazil:</strong> the rights of the LGPD, including confirmation of processing,
      anonymization or elimination of unnecessary data, information about sharing, review of
      automated decisions, and the right to complain to the ANPD.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>United States:</strong> where state privacy laws apply, the right to know, correct,
      delete, and port your data, to opt out of the sale or sharing of personal information and of
      targeted advertising, and to non-discrimination for exercising these rights. The tracking
      consent in iOS Settings is the most direct opt-out for ad-related sharing.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Because we hold no account for you, exercising these rights works by email: write to
    <a href="mailto:contact@rubenspessoa.dev">contact@rubenspessoa.dev</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Our apps are not directed at children under 14 (or under 13 in the United States), and we do
    not knowingly collect data from them. If you believe a child has provided us data, contact us
    and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we change this policy, we will update it here with a new effective date and, as far as
    technically and legally feasible, notify you in the affected app. Where changes affect
    processing based on your consent, we will collect new consent where required.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
